meta {
  name: Space Get Repo
  type: http
  seq: 156
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/xrpc/com.atproto.space.getRepo?space=at://did:plc:authorityaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa/space/org.example.bucket/main&repo={{did}}
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{accessToken}}
}

params:query {
  space: at://did:plc:authorityaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa/space/org.example.bucket/main
  repo: {{did}}
  ~excludeValues: false
}

docs {
  Download a permissioned repo as a CAR file for full-state recovery. The CAR declares two
  roots in order — the signed commit, then a DRISL (DAG-CBOR) index mapping
  "{collection}/{rkey}" to record CID in canonical DAG-CBOR key order (length-first, then
  bytewise) — followed by the record blocks in the index's order, so it verifies while
  streaming. Blobs are not included (fetch via space.getBlob).

  "excludeValues=true" writes only the two roots; the index still authenticates against the
  commit (the set hash folds from index entries), so a syncer can diff it against a local copy
  and fetch just the records it lacks.
}
